    middle: 'Fast discussions, recorded media, lab instructions, and teachers speaking while facing the board can create barriers across subjects.',
    impacts: ['English vocabulary and syntax may need teaching, based on the student’s language history.', 'Provide clear models of academic English while valuing the student’s language.', 'Interpret math vocabulary and word-problem language accessibly.', 'Watching an interpreter, teacher, and slide at once divides visual attention.', 'Missed cues may look like refusal; check access first.', 'Use the established language and interpreter arrangements.', 'Build turn-taking and sight lines into peer discussion.'],
    strategies: ['Face the class and identify who is speaking.', 'Use one speaker at a time with visible turn-taking.', 'Provide accurate captions and transcripts for media.', 'Share vocabulary and materials with the interpreter in advance.', 'Pause between showing a visual and explaining it.', 'Check understanding through a response rather than a yes/no hearing question.'],
